module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.native_stack_recursion_unbounded_over_corpus_shaped_structure

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data native_stack_recursion_unbounded_over_corpus_shaped_structure: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "native_stack_recursion_unbounded_over_corpus_shaped_structure" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a walk whose native-stack depth grows with the depth of corpus-shaped data, with no declared bound** (the compiler recurses once per level of a structure whose depth is an input, not a constant. Past some corpus the process aborts on stack exhaustion. HARM: the abort is not a diagnostic -- it is a SIGSEGV turned into `thread ... has overflowed its stack` and an abort, so it carries no span, no diagnostic identity, and no partial result. It lands OUTSIDE the ladder entirely rather than low on it: the run neither succeeds nor refuses, and every downstream reader sees a crashed process rather than a located refusal. Worse, the abort is silent about its own cause -- it kills the process before the summary line, so the very output that would characterise the input is the output you lose. ",

    "**THE DISTINGUISHING FACT IS THAT THE RECURSION NEED NOT APPEAR IN OUR SOURCE AT ALL.** The class has two instances and they differ in exactly this, which is why one row covers both and why looking only for authored recursion finds half of it. ",

    "AUTHORED INSTANCE: `v1.compiler.infer_types` `node_type_shape` and `node_type_shape_argument_list` are mutually recursive over type structure with no depth bound, rendering `Primitive(...)`, `Named(...)`, `Product(...)`, `Coproduct(...)` by descending into children. A reader can find this one, and grep for `fn` names finds it. ",

    "COMPILER-GENERATED INSTANCE: `v1.std.core` `Node` carries `children: Rc<Vec<Rc<Node>>>` (and `params`, `uses`, `properties`, `body`, `type_annotation` likewise) with no hand-written `Drop`, so the DESTRUCTOR rustc synthesises recurses once per level on every release of a deep graph. **No reading of our own source can find it, because it is not in our source.** Grepping for recursion, auditing every `fn`, and eliminating every in-window candidate by inspection all report health -- and did, on the specimen below, where three code candidates in the failing window were correctly eliminated by reading while the actual recursion was in glue no one had written. ",

    "**RECOGNITION RULE, and it is about the DATA, not about the code: any type whose values are trees or chains of unbounded depth carries this class in every operation that touches a whole value -- including the ones you did not write.** Construction, traversal, rendering, cloning, comparison, hashing, serialisation and RELEASE are all depth-recursive by default. The question to ask of a recursive carrier is not `which of my functions recurse` but `what happens to a value of this type at 10^6 levels`, and the honest answer is usually that nobody knows because nobody has one. ",

    "**RECEIPT, EXECUTED, WITH A PAIRED CONTROL AND ONE CHANGED LINE** (2026-09-05, quick-heron-85, during the NS-N containment cut). A two-file subject -- `std.measure` plus `test.claim.long.reference_closure_equivalence_test`, compiled with `src/v2` and `src/v1` as name-pool roots -- aborts with `stack overflow` after four pipeline phases and before its diagnostic summary prints. ",

    "THE STACK-THRESHOLD INSTRUMENT TURNS THE BINARY INTO A SCALAR: bisecting `ulimit -s` gives the minimum stack at which each configuration completes. Each file ALONE completes at 1024 KiB; the PAIR completes at 147456 KiB and overflows at 139264 KiB. A factor of at least 144, closed on both sides, which is what establishes the recursion as FINITE AND DEEP rather than unbounded-in-the-limit -- an unlimited stack completes. ",

    "THE DISCRIMINATOR IS THE ONE-LINE PROBE, not the threshold: `std::mem::forget(resolved.clone())` at the head of `v1.compiler.compile` `emit_resolved_for_target_selected`, holding files, binary invocation, source roots, stack size and diagnostics fixed and changing ONLY whether the tree is ever released. Paired at the same stock 8192 KiB: unpatched OVERFLOW, leaked binary exit 1, zero `stack overflow`, and the summary line prints (496 blocking, 2643 advisory). The destructor was the recursion. ",

    "**THE PROBE MUST FORGET A CLONE, NOT THE VALUE**, and this is the part worth carrying to the next investigator: `resolved` is an `Rc`, so forgetting IT merely drops one handle and moves the destructor to whoever holds the last one -- reading as a false PERSIST and killing a true hypothesis. Forgetting a CLONE pins the outer refcount above zero, so the contents can never be released no matter who else holds a handle. That converts `check the precondition` into `remove the failure mode`, which is the difference between a probe you have to trust and one that cannot lie. ",

    "**WHAT DID NOT DISCRIMINATE, recorded because each looked decisive and cost a cycle:** diagnostic COUNT is blind -- a probe rendering 8,000 diagnostics does not overflow while this configuration's 3,139 does; per-diagnostic SHAPE is blind unless the shape is in the graph; and a 2,000-level-deep authored expression chain completes. The depth that matters is the depth of the structure RELEASED, which no probe varying the diagnostic list can reach. ",

    "**RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder.** A stack-exhaustion abort is not a mitigated failure -- there is no typed outcome, no located diagnostic, and no bound. Section 5's floor is that a wrong or impossible path fails LOUDLY AND TYPED; a SIGSEGV is loud in the wrong register, carrying no subject and no location, and it is the arm section 4b explicitly places outside the ladder rather than on its bottom rung. ",

    "**CEILING: structurally impossible, and it is attainable, because depth is decidable at construction.** Nothing here is undecidable and nothing waits on external reality. ",

    "**THE REPAIR MAY NOT BE A BIGGER STACK, A FATTER THREAD, OR A RAISED BUDGET, AND THE LEAK IS AN INSTRUMENT RATHER THAN AN ARM.** All four leave the abort exactly where it was and move the corpus at which it fires, which is section 5's absorbing fallback in its purest form: the failure arm WIDENS instead of refusing, the widening is denominated in the corpus rather than the change, and the deficit stops ranking for repair because the symptom moved. The two honest arms are a release and traversal whose depth does not grow with the data -- an explicit iterative teardown and an explicit worklist walk -- or a DECLARED depth bound enforced at construction, refusing a too-deep structure with a typed, located diagnostic naming the carrier and the level. ",

    "**NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, and it names a CAPABILITY rather than a repair to one carrier:** a mechanism that derives, from a declared carrier, whether any operation on it -- including generated ones -- can recurse without a bound, so that authoring an unbounded-depth carrier without an iterative release or a declared bound fails to compile. Repairing `Node` alone does not retire this row; it removes one instance, and `node_type_shape` would still stand, as would every carrier authored tomorrow. ",

    "**BOUNDED AGAINST TWO NEIGHBOURS.** Section 5's absorbing fallback is a mechanism that WIDENS when it cannot answer precisely; here nothing widens and nothing is answered -- the process dies. And `right_censored_cost_read_as_exact` concerns a measurement truncated by a limit; the resemblance is superficial, because there the run completes and reports a bounded number, whereas here the limit destroys the run and its report together, which is precisely why the threshold instrument had to be built to get any number at all. ",

    "**THE POPULATION ON MAIN IS UNMEASURED AND THE ROW DOES NOT CLAIM OTHERWISE, WHICH IS A DENOMINATOR FACT AND NOT BOOKKEEPING** (established 2026-09-06, after this row was first written, by the three-cell probe that identified what builds the chain). THE SOLE SPECIMEN WAS PRODUCED BY A RESOLVER RULE THAT IS NOT PRESENT ON MAIN: under main and under the merge base, the deepest structure this same instrument observes in the same corpus is 85, and admitting the one refused callable owner collapses the specimen from 1,800,008 to that same 85 with the deepest site moving to an unrelated module. **WHETHER ORDINARY CORPUS GROWTH ALONE CAN REACH COMPARABLE DEPTH IS UNMEASURED, AND NOBODY HAS SHOWN THAT IT CAN.** THE PRODUCING DEFECT IS NAMED SO THE TWO ROWS CONNECT RATHER THAN LEAVING THE NEXT READER TO RE-DERIVE IT: the depth was reached because an UNRESOLVABLE CALL WAS ELABORATED RATHER THAN REFUSED, which is filed as the call-site form of `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.state_space_conflation` -- the callable-lookup carrier collapses builtin, locally-bound and genuinely-missing into one constructor, and the consumer reads that collapsed absence as affirmative formal authority. ",

    "**STATED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS, BECAUSE EACH HALF GUARDS AGAINST THE OPPOSITE MISREAD.** A reader must not conclude that corpus growth alone reaches this depth -- that is the unmeasured half above. A reader must ALSO not conclude that the structure was a harness artefact: NOTHING WAS FORCED IN THE RUN THAT PRODUCED IT. The 1,800,008 baseline is an ordinary compile under an ordinary resolver rule; the forced admissions were the two PROBES placed either side of that baseline to identify its cause. The structure was real, an accepted compile built it, and the class it exhibits is independent of whichever defect supplied the depth -- which is why this row stands on its own and does not wait on that defect's repair. ",

    "**THE SECOND DEFECT THIS SPECIMEN EXPOSES IS NOT THIS ROW AND MUST NOT BE ABSORBED INTO IT:** nothing in two source files is 10^5 levels deep, so some pipeline stage BUILDS a structure far deeper than its input -- a chain where a flat structure was intended. That is a separate defect, for which this class is only the reporter, and it will be pathological for every consumer that walks the structure rather than only the one that releases it.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
